+### [Interblock Interpolation](11155-interblock-interpolation.md)
+Interblock Interpolation is a data reduction technique used in GPU-based volume ray casting to handle missing samples between spatial blocks, allowing for significantly higher compression ratios than standard replication methods. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Nearest Neighbor Sampling](11694-nearest-neighbor-sampling.md) by explicitly reconstructing values in empty regions through interpolation rather than simple replication or discarding, thereby enabling data reductions of up to 80:1 while maintaining visual continuity.
+
 ### [Lanczos Resampling](11246-lanczos-resampling.md)
 Lanczos resampling is an interpolation technique used to resample (downsample or upsample) volumetric data by replacing each selected sample with a translated copy of the Lanczos kernel, which is a limited Sinc function. It sets itself apart from linear or cubic interpolation by offering a sharper frequency response with reduced aliasing, at the cost of a wider support radius and higher computational complexity. It builds on [Interpolation Methods](10526-interpolation-methods.md).
